  "finalText": "The ÉCLAT reveal is built, but the type still renders in a sans-serif, not the serif you asked for. I set \"Cormorant Garamond\" first, then \"Playfair Display\". Neither shows in the preview, so both look like they fell back to the default font. I haven't tried a third font. If you have a serif installed, tell me its name and I'll switch it.\n\nIt runs 7 seconds at 1080×1920 on a near-black background (#0a0908). I haven't run the critic, and I checked it only in contact-sheet and still frames, not played back in real time.\n\n- **Gold line:** a thin vertical champagne line (**Gold Line**) draws itself from 0.6 s to 3.8 s with a Sine In Out ease, so it starts and stops softly.\n- **Name:** **ECLAT Name** fades in one letter at a time from 2 s. Each letter takes 1.6 s and they step 0.4 s apart. It is set wide-tracked in gold.\n- **Tracking tightening:** letter spacing can't be animated here, so the name eases from 106% down to 100% scale over four seconds. That reads as a slight settling inward, not a true tracking change.\n- **Subtitle:** **Eau de Parfum** is a small, muted gold line that fades in slowly from 4.4 s to 6 s.\n- **Ending:** the last second is a held end card, with plenty of empty space around the lockup.\n\nI can make it slower or add a slow glow on the line's tip."
